"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Asking for something inconvenient"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"You must…"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"An obligation"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Rules and safety, rarely person-to-person"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"You should…"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Advice"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Recommending, not requiring"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"I have to…"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"An obligation on you"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Explaining why you cannot do something"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Modals — how firm you are being"}]]}]
1e:["$","div","5",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-primary-200 bg-primary-50/50 p-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-700 mb-2","children":"Worked example"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1","children":"Turning a demand into a request"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"You need a coworker to swap a shift with you."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":1}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Avoid the bare imperative: not \"Swap shifts with me Thursday.\""}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"In English an imperative to a peer sounds like an order. Many languages use a direct form politely; English marks politeness with modals instead, so the direct form reads as rudeness even when none is meant."}]]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":2}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Use \"could\" and add the reason: \"Could you swap Thursday with me? I have a class that evening.\""}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"\"Could\" makes it a request rather than an instruction, and the reason gives them something to say yes to. English speakers expect a short reason with a request between peers."}]]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":3}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Give them a way to say no: \"If it doesn't work, no problem — I'll ask Marcus.\""}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"This removes the pressure and makes a yes genuine. It also protects the relationship, which matters more than this one shift."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-primary-200 text-gray-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Result: "}],"A request they can accept or decline without awkwardness."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-gray-900 font-medium","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"🔑 "}],"Could + reason + an easy way out. That is the standard shape of an English workplace request."]}]]}]
1f:["$","$L23","6",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"Your supervisor asks if you are available Saturday. You are willing but would prefer not to. What should you say?","options":["\"I will work Saturday.\"","\"I could work Saturday if you need me.\"","\"I work Saturday.\"","\"I am working Saturday.\""],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"\"Could\" makes it an offer rather than a commitment, and \"if you need me\" signals that you are available without volunteering. The others all state, in different tenses, that you are working — and your supervisor will schedule you.","optionRationales":["\"Will\" is a commitment. Your supervisor will take it as settled.","Correct. An offer, with a condition attached.","The simple present states it as a regular fact — it sounds like Saturday is normally your day.","The present continuous states it as already arranged."]}}]
20:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-[40px] sm:leading-[1.05]","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Focus on the forms that change meaning."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write six sentences about your own work using each tense in the table once."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Rewrite these as polite requests: \"Give me the schedule.\" \"Tell me when you finish.\" \"Change my shift.\""}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write one sentence committing to something and one offering it, and mark the difference."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Listen for \"could you\" and \"would you mind\" over one day and note who says them and when."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
